WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.799
This work is pretty major from the point

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.820
of view that's not just putting in traffic signals.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:10.240
It's also replacing and upgrading

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.380
sewer pipes, storm water pipes and water mains

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.690
So it's a pretty major piece of work.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.160
We suggest commuters look at

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.500
alternative routes to avoid the intersection

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.880
because the more traffic that uses the intersection,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.200
the more delays there'll be.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.560
Some of those alternatives are

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.820
for people living on the west side of Rangiora

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.160
there's the Fernside / Flaxton / Townsend road link.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.540
And that provides a direct

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.020
connection into the western side of Rangiora

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.480
For the east and north,

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.240
there's possibly using Rangiora-Woodend Road

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.720
as a route that will avoid Southbrook Road.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.420
So they're the two main routes that

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.560
people should consider.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.140
If people have use the intersection, then we'd suggest

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:53.550
they avoid the peak time and peak times are:

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.840
at school start and finish times.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.070
And also from about four o'clock onwards

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.610
in the evenings, it gets pretty congested

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.990
So it's just avoiding those times if you can.

